# 🗼 AETHERIA — DUNGEON SYSTEM

> **The Tower is not merely a dungeon.**
>
> **It is the final surviving structure between the Master and the end of the world.**
>
> Every floor contains a fragment of the world that once existed.
>
> Some floors are battlefields.
> Some are ruins.
> Some are cities.
> Some are forgotten civilizations.
> Some are memories of the world before its destruction.
>
> **To climb the Tower is to walk through the remains of Aetheria.**

---

# 1. DUNGEON SYSTEM OVERVIEW

The **Dungeon System** manages the entire Tower of Rebirth.

The Tower contains:

```text
100 FLOORS
```

The Tower is the primary progression path of the Master.

The Dungeon System manages:

```text
Tower
Floor
Dungeon
Dungeon Session
Floor Environment
Floor Story
Floor Objective
Floor Event Trigger
Boss
Raid Boss
World Exploration
Pre-Destruction Exploration
Dungeon Mission
Floor Reward Context
Floor State
Floor Difficulty
Destruction Level
Dungeon Completion
Party Deployment
Party Lock
Mission Failure
Mission Victory
Forced Mission Resolution
Party Death
Permanent Death Resolution
```

The Dungeon System **does not directly manage Enemy generation**.

Enemy generation, composition, statistics, behavior, scaling, and encounter difficulty are handled by:

# **ENEMY SYSTEM**

The Dungeon System only provides the environment and conditions required by the Enemy System.

```text
DUNGEON SYSTEM
      │
      ├── Floor
      ├── Environment
      ├── Mission
      ├── Difficulty Context
      └── Enemy Spawn Condition
                  │
                  ▼
             ENEMY SYSTEM
                  │
                  ├── Enemy Type
                  ├── Enemy Count
                  ├── Enemy Level
                  ├── Enemy Stats
                  ├── Enemy Behavior
                  └── Enemy Formation
```

