# 2. ABSOLUTE DUNGEON COMMITMENT RULE

Once a Party enters a Dungeon Mission:

# **THE PARTY IS PERMANENTLY COMMITTED TO THE MISSION.**

There is no normal command, menu, skill, item, or Master action that can forcibly return the Party to the Lobby or Town.

```text
PARTY
  ↓
ENTER DUNGEON
  ↓
MISSION START
  ↓
PARTY LOCK
  ↓
NO MANUAL RECALL
  ↓
MISSION ACTIVE
```

The Master cannot manually:

```text
Recall Party
Return Party to Lobby
Return Party to Town
Cancel Mission
Exit Dungeon
Teleport Party Outside
Replace Party
Remove Hero
Transfer Hero
Disband Party
Change Party Leader
```

The Party must remain inside the Dungeon until the mission reaches a valid final resolution.

The only valid mission resolutions are:

```text
MISSION VICTORY
MISSION FAILURE
PARTY DEATH
SPECIAL SYSTEM-MANDATED ESCAPE
EMERGENCY EVENT
DUNGEON FORCED EXIT
```

However, these exits are not controlled by the Master.

They can only occur when the Dungeon System, Floor configuration, Event System, or another authorized system produces a valid result.

```text
MASTER COMMAND
"RETURN TO TOWN"
        ↓
      DENIED
        ↓
MISSION CONTINUES
```

---

# 3. NO MANUAL ESCAPE

The Dungeon does not contain a normal exit command.

The following actions are permanently unavailable while a mission is active:

```text
EXIT DUNGEON
RETURN TO LOBBY
RETURN TO TOWN
RECALL PARTY
CANCEL MISSION
ABANDON MISSION
TELEPORT OUT
FORCE PARTY RETREAT
```

Example:

```text
MISSION ACTIVE
      │
      ├── EXIT DUNGEON       = BLOCKED
      ├── RETURN TO TOWN     = BLOCKED
      ├── RECALL PARTY      = BLOCKED
      ├── REPLACE HERO      = BLOCKED
      └── CANCEL MISSION    = BLOCKED
```

If the Master attempts to issue a forbidden command:

> **"Master, forced withdrawal is not permitted. The Party is bound to the active Dungeon Mission."**

The mission continues regardless of the Master’s desire to retreat.

---

# 4. MISSION COMPLETION REQUIREMENT

Every deployed Party must remain inside the Dungeon until one of the following occurs:

```text
Mission Objective Completed
Mission Objective Failed
All Party Heroes Dead
Time Limit Reached
Special Floor Condition Resolved
System-Mandated Escape Triggered
```

The Party cannot return to the Lobby or Town simply because:

```text
The battle is difficult
The Party is injured
The Master changes strategy
The Master regrets deployment
The Party has low resources
The Party has lost its Leader
The Party has lost some Heroes
The Master wants to use another Party
```

The Party must continue until the Dungeon produces a final result.

