# 5. PARTY DEATH RULE

A Dungeon Party has a permanent combat state during the mission.

Example:

```text
PARTY 1

Hero A — Alive
Hero B — Alive
Hero C — Alive
Hero D — Alive
Hero E — Alive
```

If one Hero dies:

```text
Hero A — DEAD
Hero B — Alive
Hero C — Alive
Hero D — Alive
Hero E — Alive
```

The Party can continue if surviving Heroes remain and the Dungeon Mission allows continuation.

However:

# **IF ALL PARTY MEMBERS DIE, THE PARTY IS DEFEATED.**

```text
Hero A — DEAD
Hero B — DEAD
Hero C — DEAD
Hero D — DEAD
Hero E — DEAD
        ↓
PARTY DEFEATED
        ↓
MISSION FAILED
        ↓
QUEST FAILED
```

The Party is not returned to the Lobby or Town after defeat.

The Party remains inside the Dungeon until the Dungeon System completes the failure resolution.

```text
ALL HEROES DEAD
        ↓
PARTY DEFEATED
        ↓
MISSION FAILURE
        ↓
DEATH RESOLUTION
        ↓
DUNGEON SESSION CLOSED
```

If the setting does not provide a valid revival system, the dead Heroes remain dead.

---

# 6. FAILURE MEANS DEATH

The core Dungeon rule is:

# **IF THE PARTY FAILS, THE PARTY DIES.**

A failed mission does not function as a safe retreat.

```text
MISSION FAILURE
        ↓
PARTY DEATH
        ↓
DUNGEON SESSION ENDS
```

The Master cannot choose:

```text
Mission Failed
     ↓
Return Safely to Town
```

Instead:

```text
Mission Failed
     ↓
Party Defeated
     ↓
Heroes Dead
     ↓
Death State Saved
```

Unless a specific Floor, Event, Artifact, or System rule provides a valid survival condition, failure results in the death of the deployed Party.

---

# 7. FAILURE RESOLUTION

When a mission failure condition is triggered:

```text
MISSION FAILURE DETECTED
        ↓
CHECK SURVIVING HEROES
        ↓
CHECK VALID ESCAPE CONDITION
        ↓
CHECK REVIVAL CONDITION
        ↓
CHECK FLOOR-SPECIFIC RULE
        ↓
RESOLVE PARTY FATE
```

Default result:

```text
NO VALID ESCAPE
NO VALID REVIVAL
        ↓
PARTY DEATH
        ↓
ALL DEPLOYED HEROES = DEAD
```

The Dungeon System must not automatically return the Party to:

```text
Lobby
Town
Base
Safe Zone
Party Selection
```

---

# 8. VALID EXCEPTIONS TO DEATH

A failed mission results in death by default.

A different result is only possible if explicitly defined by the system.

Valid exceptions may include:

```text
System-Mandated Escape
Emergency Event
Floor-Specific Escape Mechanic
Artifact-Based Survival
External Rescue Event
Story-Defined Intervention
Revival Mechanic
Dungeon Collapse Teleport
```

These exceptions cannot be activated manually by the Master.

Example:

```text
MISSION FAILURE
        ↓
FLOOR HAS EMERGENCY ESCAPE EVENT
        ↓
EVENT SYSTEM TRIGGER
        ↓
PARTY SURVIVES
        ↓
SYSTEM FORCED EXIT
```

Without an explicit exception:

```text
MISSION FAILURE
        ↓
PARTY DEATH
```

