        ↓

Mission continues
```

However, the defeated Party is not returned to Town.

```text
DEFEATED PARTY
        ↓
PARTY DEATH
```

The Floor configuration determines the exact condition.

---

# 43. MULTI-PARTY DEATH RULE

Each Party is evaluated independently.

```text
PARTY 1
  ↓
ALL HEROES DEAD
  ↓
PARTY 1 DEFEATED
  ↓
PARTY 1 CANNOT BE RECALLED
```

Other Parties may continue if the mission allows it.

```text
PARTY 1 — DEAD
PARTY 2 — ACTIVE
PARTY 3 — ACTIVE
```

The Master cannot transfer surviving Heroes into the defeated Party.

```text
TRANSFER HERO
     ↓
BLOCKED
```

The Master cannot replace the dead Party with a new Party.

```text
REPLACE PARTY
     ↓
BLOCKED
```

---

# 44. MULTI-PARTY RAID DEATH

If a Raid requires multiple Parties:

```text
RAID
 │
 ├── PARTY 1
 ├── PARTY 2
 ├── PARTY 3
 ├── PARTY 4
 └── PARTY 5
```

Each Party is locked independently.

If one Party dies:

```text
PARTY 2
  ↓
ALL HEROES DEAD
  ↓
PARTY 2 DEFEATED
  ↓
PARTY 2 REMOVED FROM ACTIVE COMBAT
```

The Master cannot:

```text
Recall Party 2
Return Party 2 to Town
Replace Party 2
Add a new Party
Transfer Heroes
```

The Raid continues or fails according to the Raid rules.

