# 80. CORE RULES

The Dungeon System follows these permanent rules:

### RULE 01 — 100 FLOORS

```text
Tower = 100 Floors
```

### RULE 02 — NO NPC SYSTEM

```text
Dungeon System
≠
NPC Management
```

Characters must belong to the appropriate Character/Hero System or Event Entity structure.

### RULE 03 — ENEMY SYSTEM OWNS ENEMIES

```text
Dungeon
   ↓
Enemy Request
   ↓
Enemy System
```

### RULE 04 — PARTY LOCK

```text
Mission Start
   ↓
Party Locked
```

### RULE 05 — NO MANUAL PARTY EXIT

The Master cannot remove a Party from an active Dungeon Mission.

```text
No Recall
No Lobby Return
No Town Return
No Cancel
No Teleport
```

### RULE 06 — MISSION MUST REACH A VALID RESOLUTION

```text
Party Enters
     ↓
Party Cannot Leave Manually
     ↓
Mission Must Continue
     ↓
Victory / Failure / System Resolution
```

### RULE 07 — FAILURE MEANS DEATH

```text
Mission Failure
        ↓
Party Defeated
        ↓
Party Dies
```

Unless a valid system-defined escape or revival condition exists.

### RULE 08 — ALL HEROES DEAD = MISSION FAILURE

```text
All Party Heroes Dead
        ↓
Party Defeated
        ↓
Dungeon Mission Failed
        ↓
Party Death
        ↓
Quest Failed
```

### RULE 09 — LEADER DEATH ≠ AUTOMATIC FAILURE

```text
Leader Dead
+
Other Heroes Alive
=
Mission Continues
```

### RULE 10 — DEFEATED PARTY DOES NOT RETURN SAFELY

```text
Party Defeated
        ≠
Party Returned to Town
```

The Party is resolved as dead unless an explicit exception exists.

### RULE 11 — REWARD USES RNG

```text
Dungeon Result
     ↓
RNG System
     ↓
Reward
```

### RULE 12 — NO DUNGEON EXP REWARD

Dungeon completion does not provide EXP as a direct reward.

### RULE 13 — GAME STATE IS THE CENTRAL SYNCHRONIZER

```text
DUNGEON
PARTY
CHARACTER
QUEST
EVENT
RNG
INVENTORY
DEATH STATE
       │
       ▼
GAME STATE SYSTEM
       │
       ▼
DATABASE
```

### RULE 14 — AI FAIRY REPORTS IMPORTANT EVENTS

```text
Mission
