# 81. FINAL DESIGN PRINCIPLE

The Dungeon System is not simply a collection of combat stages.

Each Floor represents a fragment of Aetheria.

The Master provides the strategy.

The Party enters the mission.

Once the mission starts, the Party becomes permanently committed to the mission.

There is no forced return to the Lobby or Town.

```text
MASTER
   ↓
SELECT PARTY
   ↓
ENTER FLOOR
   ↓
PARTY LOCK
   ↓
NO MANUAL EXIT
   ↓
MISSION
   ↓
COMBAT / EXPLORATION
   ↓
ENEMY SYSTEM
   ↓
EVENT
   ↓
BOSS / RAID
   ↓
VICTORY / FAILURE
   │
   ├── VICTORY
   │      ↓
   │   PARTY SURVIVES
   │      ↓
   │   REWARD
   │
   └── FAILURE
          ↓
      PARTY DIES
          ↓
      DEATH STATE SAVED
```

The Master cannot simply remove a Party when the situation becomes dangerous.

The Master cannot return the Party to the Lobby.

The Master cannot return the Party to Town.

The Master cannot cancel the mission.

The Heroes must face the consequences of the mission.

```text
PARTY ENTERS
     ↓
NO MANUAL EXIT
     ↓
HEROES FIGHT
     ↓
HEROES SURVIVE
     │
     └──────────────► VICTORY

OR

HEROES FALL
     ↓
ALL HEROES DEAD
     ↓
PARTY DEFEATED
     ↓
MISSION FAILED
     ↓
PARTY DIES
     ↓
QUEST FAILED
```

The Dungeon therefore becomes a real strategic risk.

Every deployment matters.

Every Hero matters.

Every Party decision matters.

And when the Master sends a Party into the Tower:

> **There is no simple "exit" button.**

> **There is no safe retreat to the Lobby or Town.**

> **The Party must finish the mission—or die inside it.**
